# ZvenFit — core rules

Static site. Markup started as a Webflow export; Webflow is no longer used, so edit `public/` directly.
Source: `public/`, `scripts/`, `functions/`. **Never edit `dist/`.**

After changes: `npm run build` or `npm run dev:watch`.

## APIs (injected at build)

- Lead: `functions/lead-intake/` → `window.ZVENFIT_LEAD_API`
- Schedule: `functions/fitbase-schedule/` → `window.ZVENFIT_SCHEDULE_API`
- Page views: `functions/site-traffic/` → `window.ZVENFIT_TRAFFIC_API`

## Build markers

HTML contains `<!-- ZvenFit: ... -->` comments replaced by `scripts/build-static.cjs`.
Edit snippets in `scripts/snippets/` or configs — not every HTML copy.

## Brand

Keep green `#00d10e`, Roadrage + Roboto. See `TODO.md` "Out of scope".

## Secrets

No tokens in HTML/JS. Use env / GitHub Secrets only.

## Verify

`npm run lint` and `npm run test:build`. Full guide: `AGENTS.md`.

## Deploy

**Frontend (`zvenfit-frontend` bucket):** only via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/main.yml`).
Do **not** manually upload to `zvenfit-frontend` (`yc storage s3api put-object`, `aws s3 cp/sync`, etc.) unless the user explicitly asks.

A push to `main` deploys production: CI runs `npm run build` and `s3 sync ./dist`. Work on a branch and open a pull request.

**Assets bucket (`zvenfit`):** coach images and static CDN assets — not deployed by CI; manual ops only when the user requests or approves.
